## 📂 Project-Specific Rules

### C Projects (00, 01, 02, 03)
- **Naming:** `ft_functionname` for libft functions
- **Headers:** Include guards with `#ifndef FT_*.H`
- **Bonus:** Create separate `*_bonus.c` files
- **Testing:** Create test files in separate directory if not prohibited
- **⚠️ MANDATORY:** Follow Norma 42 v4.1 (see strict rules above)

### C++ Projects (04) - NO NORMA 42 v4.1 REQUIRED
- **Naming:** `CapitalCamelCase` for classes, `snake_case` for methods
- **Headers:** Use `.hpp` extension
- **Const correctness:** Mark immutable methods as `const`
- **Orthodox Canonical Form:** Implement all 4 required methods
- **No STL restrictions:** Use C++ standard library
- **✅ Flexible formatting** - No 80-col limit, functions can be >25 lines

### 42 School C++ Modules (CPP00-CPP04)

**Compiler & Standards:**
- **Mandatory:** C++98 standard (`-std=c++98`)
- **Compiler:** `c++` command (g++ or clang++)
- **Flags:** `-Wall -Wextra -Werror -std=c++98`
- **❌ Forbidden:** C++11 features (auto, nullptr, range-based for, etc.)

**Module Structure:**
Each module contains 3-4 exercises (ex00, ex01, ex02, ex03):
```
CPP0X/
├── Makefile              # Multi-exercise template
├── README.md             # Professional module documentation
├── ex00/
│   ├── *.hpp             # Header files
│   ├── *.cpp             # Implementation files
│   └── main.cpp          # Entry point
├── ex01/
│   └── [similar structure]
├── ex02/
│   └── [similar structure]
└── ex03/
    └── [similar structure]
```

**Key Requirements by Module:**

**CPP00 - Introduction to OOP**
- ✅ Basic classes, constructors, destructors
- ✅ Member functions (methods)
- ✅ Encapsulation (public, private, protected)
- ✅ Use of std::string, std::cout, std::cin

**CPP01 - Memory, Pointers & References**
- ✅ Pointers and references fundamentals
- ✅ new/delete operators (no malloc/free)
- ✅ File I/O (std::fstream)
- ✅ String manipulation

**CPP02 - Operator Overloading & Orthodox Canonical Form**
- ✅ **Mandatory:** Orthodox Canonical Form (4 methods):
  - Default constructor
  - Copy constructor
  - Copy assignment operator
  - Destructor
- ✅ Operator overloading (arithmetic, comparison, stream operators)
- ✅ Fixed-point number implementation (const fields, subject requirements)
- ✅ Static methods and members

**CPP03 - Inheritance**
- ✅ Single inheritance with virtual inheritance for multiple inheritance
- ✅ Constructor chaining (member initializer lists)
- ✅ Diamond Problem solution
- ✅ Protected and private inheritance
- ✅ Virtual destructors

**CPP04 - Polymorphism & Design Patterns**
- ✅ Virtual functions and pure virtual functions (abstract classes)
- ✅ Interfaces (pure virtual methods)
- ✅ Factory Pattern implementation
- ✅ Dynamic casting (when appropriate)
- ✅ Polymorphic behavior with inheritance hierarchies

**Orthodox Canonical Form Enforcement:**
All classes must implement OCF (especially from CPP02 onward):
```cpp
class MyClass
{
private:
    int	value;

public:
    MyClass();                          // Default constructor
    MyClass(const MyClass &other);      // Copy constructor
    MyClass &operator=(const MyClass &other);  // Copy assignment
    ~MyClass();                         // Destructor
    
    // Other methods...
};
```

**Compilation & Makefile:**
- Use `Makefile.cpp.multi` template for module structure
- Each exercise compiles to separate executable
- Object files in `obj/` directory
- All targets: `all`, `ex00`, `ex01`, `ex02`, `ex03`, `clean`, `fclean`, `re`
- Optional: `debug`, `release`, `valgrind` targets

**Code Style (C++98):**
- ✅ Method declarations in headers (`.hpp`)
- ✅ Method definitions in implementation files (`.cpp`)
- ✅ Use of initialization lists for constructors
- ✅ Proper use of `const` for methods and parameters
- ✅ Avoid C++11 auto, nullptr, uniform initialization
- ✅ Traditional for loops instead of range-based
- ✅ Use std:: namespace or `using std::type;` declarations

**Testing & Validation:**
- ✅ Compile with all warning flags: `c++ -Wall -Wextra -Werror -std=c++98`
- ✅ Test each exercise independently
- ✅ Verify Orthodox Canonical Form with copy/assignment
- ✅ Check for memory leaks: `valgrind --leak-check=full ./ex00`
- ✅ Ensure no undefined behavior

**Common Pitfalls to Avoid:**
- ❌ Using C++11 features (auto, nullptr, lambdas, etc.)
- ❌ Forgetting copy constructor/assignment operator
- ❌ Not implementing virtual destructors in inheritance
- ❌ Memory leaks from new/delete
- ❌ Forgetting const on const methods
- ❌ Deep copy issues in copy constructor
- ❌ Self-assignment check missing in copy assignment



### Graphics Projects (so_long, others)
- **Minilibx:** Use provided library, no external graphics libs
- **Memory:** Free all resources including textures, windows
- **Window handling:** Handle window close events properly

### Concurrency Projects (philosophers, etc)
- **Thread safety:** Use mutex/semaphore correctly
- **Race conditions:** Check with tools like `helgrind` (valgrind)
- **Deadlock prevention:** Document lock order
- **Resource cleanup:** Ensure all threads join before exit

